0..78 Comment "//! A fold whose case sits beneath a parameter after the one it recurses on is"
79..155 Comment "//! read as the fixpoint, as one with the case at its root is. Programs that"
156..232 Comment "//! only store, quotiented by state\'s put-put law, are folded by passing the"
233..313 Comment "//! state: at `Store(s, Store(u, k))` the fold runs to `final(k, u)` through two"
314..393 Comment "//! of its own calls, and at `Store(u, k)` through one, so the two sides of the"
394..471 Comment "//! law meet from one fresh initial state. The law is the algebraic theory of"
472..515 Comment "//! state\'s `put(s, put(u, k)) = put(u, k)`"
516..592 Comment "//! [Plotkin-2002-notions_computation_determine_monads], and the fold is the"
593..627 Comment "//! handler that passes the state."
628..631 Comment "//!"
632..648 Comment "//! - see: #2510"
649..713 Comment "//! - cites: [Plotkin-2002-notions_computation_determine_monads]"
714..717 Comment "//!"
718..876 Comment "//! [Plotkin-2002-notions_computation_determine_monads]: https://doi.org/10.1007/3-540-45931-6_24 \"Plotkin and Power, Notions of computation determine monads\""
878..953 Comment "/// Programs that only store, quotiented by put-put: a store the next store"
954..981 Comment "/// overwrites is no store."
